# Module D doesn't need any secret keys yet — every number on screen is
# currently made up (see electron/ipc/dashboard.ipc.ts), so there's nothing
# real to authenticate with.
#
# Once the real data sources are connected, keys may be needed for:
#
# LINKEDIN_CLIENT_ID / LINKEDIN_CLIENT_SECRET   # real post analytics (impressions, engagement, followers)
# HUBSPOT_API_KEY / PIPEDRIVE_API_TOKEN / SALESFORCE_CLIENT_ID ...   # the optional CRM push (SOW "Phase 5+" stretch goal)
#
# Where the posts, leads, and SEO numbers themselves come from depends on
# the team's decision described in modules/dashboard/services/dataSync.ts.
